#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054511 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054806 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f41c2f3b-9b55-5f32-bb0a-a8397cdf66ce" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the X- or Y-Coordinate of a Point in the Coordinate Plane"}] :question/id #uuid "e4658959-f2fb-5bb4-ad05-d75b7c74a5d5" :question/math-academy-id "e-2372" :question/problem "What is the $x$-coordinate of the point $P$?\n\n![](images/cf/cf628679e0e9726a0db5d3399d992a0333911be16b8ccd89d2d6455e540ea3d9.png)" :question/worked-solution "To find the coordinates of $P$, we start at the origin, move $3$ units *left*, and then $2$ units *up*.\n\n![](images/2d/2df77be5e817368e4082061f623ab2c10f2ec7f2ebd042864a1418e0aa67592f.png)\n\nThe coordinates of $P$ are $({\\color{red}{-3}},{\\color{blue}{2}})$. Therefore, the $x$-coordinate of $P$ is ${\\color{red}{-3}}$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054597 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054808 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e5418e0e-fff7-5d08-b915-6e87be27a132" :knowledge-point/title "Plotting a Point in the Coordinate Plane"}] :question/id #uuid "f610b8b9-8e9e-5a64-bc52-c1f939a0f147" :question/math-academy-id "e-974" :question/problem "Plot the point $C$ with coordinates $(1,-2)$ on the Cartesian plane." :question/worked-solution "Starting at the origin $O$, we move along the $x$ and $y$ axes to get to the point $C$.\n\nFirst, we move along the $x$-axis. The point $C$ has an $x$-coordinate of $1$, so we move $1$ unit to the *right*, in the *positive* direction of the $x$-axis.\n\nThen, we move along the $y$-axis. The point $C$ has a $y$-coordinate of $-2$, so we move $2$ units *down*, in the *negative* direction of the $y$-axis.\n\n![](images/49/49069b4b9be29c0a999e7d2b71eec9a973eda9ad1f8a2a7b897d76970771a644.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054598 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054807 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b509b42a-c38a-5400-8f93-f3e9024b16a2" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Coordinates of a Point"}] :question/id #uuid "bda7aaff-f03f-53bd-b114-d28a46599641" :question/math-academy-id "e-975" :question/problem "What are the $xy$-coordinates of the point $D$ shown below?\n\n![](images/c5/c546e2deb5b19c0068fd4ad550f97d3ee3143ec75bf96ca59ce5c44b825ab79e.png)" :question/worked-solution "To find the coordinates of $D$, we inspect its position along the $x$ and $y$ axes.\n\nThe point $D$ is $3$ units to the *left* of the origin, in the *negative* direction of the $x$-axis. So, $D$ has an $x$-coordinate of $-3$.\n\nAdditionally, the point $D$ is $2$ units *below* the origin, in the *negative* direction of the $y$-axis. So, $D$ has a $y$-coordinate of $-2$.\n\nThe point $D$ has an $x$-coordinate of $-3$ and a $y$-coordinate of $-2$, so its coordinates are $(-3,-2)$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054599 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054809 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7fcec0d8-ca03-5446-a42f-65d0ccddd584" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Quadrant of a Given Point"}] :question/id #uuid "419738bb-56e5-52db-aa34-42ccd945fe64" :question/math-academy-id "e-977" :question/problem "To which quadrant does the point $(4,-2)$ belong?" :question/worked-solution "In order to identify the quadrant to which the point $(4,-2)$ belongs, we start by plotting the point.\n\n- The $x$-coordinate of the point is $4$, so we move $4$ units to the right of the origin.\n- The $y$-coordinate of the point is $-2$, so we move $2$ units down from the origin.\n\n![](images/02/02b0dd5d2d125277ffb6fc637fa612eef451c06522efa7655d8374c68641e796.png)\n\nBased on the graph, we can tell that the point belongs to quadrant $\\textrm{IV}$, the fourth quadrant."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186055120 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054808 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e5418e0e-fff7-5d08-b915-6e87be27a132" :knowledge-point/title "Plotting a Point in the Coordinate Plane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:ans